#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0127A expect=violation domain=ADLBC
#note "BASE is declared and ABLFL is not, so var_exists(\"BASE\") is true and not var_exists(\"ABLFL\") is true: a presence-only check that BroadcastFold decides at dataset level, giving exactly ONE violation carrying row 1 regardless of the row count. The pin adds BASE, whose value comes from data row 1; BASEC is not declared here (omitted from the value map) and ABLFL must never be pinned - the rule fires precisely because it is absent."
#library standard=adamig version=1-3
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 BASE=1.5
dataset ADLBC structure=BDS
col STUDYID type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col PARAMCD type=Char
col AVAL    type=Num
col BASE    type=Num
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | ALT | 2.5 | 1.5
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1023 | ALT | 7.0 | 7.0
